+NPU Support Runbook (Edge TPU, OpenVINO, Inferentia, Habana, Generic)
+===================================================================
+
+Overview
+--------
+This runbook provides operator steps to enable NPU support across several vendors:
+ - Coral Edge TPU (Edge)
+ - Intel OpenVINO / Movidius VPU (Edge)
+ - AWS Inferentia (Cloud)
+ - Habana Gaudi/Goya (Cloud)
+ - Generic NPU scaffold (vendor-agnostic)
+
+High-level steps (common)
+-------------------------
+1. Provision nodes with the vendor runtime/drivers installed.
+2. Label nodes: kubectl label node <node> aegis/npu=<vendor>
+3. Deploy device plugin or privileged daemonset (if required).
+4. Compile model for target (compiler toolchain per vendor).
+5. Build serving Docker image with vendor runtime + compiled model.
+6. Deploy serving manifest with nodeSelector aegis/npu=<vendor>.
+7. Run smoke tests: compare outputs vs CPU baseline; produce signed evaluation_summary.json.
+
+Per-vendor notes
+----------------
+Edge TPU (Coral)
+- Install libedgetpu runtime on node.
+- Use edgetpu_compiler to compile .tflite -> _edgetpu.tflite.
+- Serving image must include libedgetpu.so and the compiled model.
+- Device access: hostPath /dev/bus/usb or privileged daemonset.
+
+OpenVINO (Intel VPU)
+- Install OpenVINO runtime and VPU driver on node.
+- Convert model to IR and use CPU/GPU/VPU plugin selection.
+- Use nodeSelector aegis/npu=openvino.
+
+Inferentia (AWS)
+- Use AWS Neuron SDK: neuron-cc for compile and neuron-runtime in container.
+- Use EC2 Inf1 instances (or cluster) and nodeSelector aegis/npu=inferentia.
+- Ensure IAM and Neuron drivers installed on hosts.
+
+Habana
+- Install Habana SynapseAI drivers and runtime.
+- Compile models using Habana tools (e.g., Habana Model Compiler).
+- Use nodeSelector aegis/npu=habana.
+
+Generic scaffold
+- Use TVM/ONNX/TensorRT or vendor delegate and record compile metadata in provenance.
+
+CI & gating
+----------
+- Add hardware presence gate to CI: fail if required labeled node not present.
+- Add inference correctness gate: run small test and compare outputs (tolerance).
+- Sign evaluation_summary.json with KMS and index artifact.
+
+Security & provenance
+--------------------
+- Store vendor credentials in Vault; do not commit secrets.
+- Record compiler version, flags and model hash in evidence bundle.
+- Sign compiled artifact and evaluation summary.
+
